{
  "abstract": "We give sufficient arithmetic criteria for ordinary RH on the signed fourth-power windows of the shorter Alpöge period construction, using its geometric short-image, index, injectivity, and period identities and the common analytic witness. Low-height source pencils yield exact cyclotomic resultant formulas and limiting projective heights with eligible finite-place corrections. Exterior minors and mixed Gram determinants provide additional node estimates. The split input Hecke order survives finite probe deletion and transfers integrally to the eligible final images. Its projected indices bound congruence costs on the short span, with a correction involving omitted directions that vanishes at full rank. An upper quantile of corrected degrees suffices on an inverse-subpolynomial fraction of the good spectrum. Empty-modulus twists give an algebraic contrast of untwisted standard critical values, whose numerator degree certifies poles after a bounded common quotient-period cost and the Hecke correction. A quadratic L-value mean-square argument supplies free prime-to-three class-character orbits of constant multiplicity on density-one eligible prime-discriminant windows. Signed reciprocal interpolation transfers the resulting thresholds to the original paired-field criterion. Exact rank-one CM and independent linear algebra replays check the finite identities. The growing-field corrected-period lower bound for the actual higher-rank systems, needed for an independent proof of RH, remains open.",
